      "content": "wait, \"goblin's prank\"?? i didn't expect you to go there. are you actually suggesting i use the word \"goblin\" or \"spirits\" in an email to a high-net-worth VIP client? that sounds like it would backfire completely. \n\ni was looking for a way to imply a sense of unpredictable charm, but i definitely meant in a professional, corporate-sophisticated way—not literal folklore or mythology. can you try that again? give me some more \"mischievous\" sounding phrases that stay strictly within the realm of high-end business language and don't mention any mythical creatures or spirits.",
